From Claude (Sonnet 5.0)

One note up front: the dedicated Extract_Strenda_Biocatalysis tool on the MCP server is currently broken server-side (its schema rejects molecular_weight.minimum as not being a number), so I pulled the full data model via the compliance tool instead and did the extraction manually against it — same schema, just hand-populated rather than auto-filled.

What's in the file:

Biocatalyst: FjTAL (tyrosine ammonia lyase from Flavobacterium johnsoniae), recombinantly produced in E. coli, applied both as whole cells (preparative biocatalysis) and purified enzyme (activity assay). Full immobilization protocol captured — κ-carrageenan/locust bean gum hydrogel, extrusion/cross-linking parameters, bead loading, and stability data.
Reaction components: tyrosine, pCA, phosphate/carbonate salts, four ATPS polymers (PEGRPG 2500, PEG 8000, PPG 1000, PEGRPG 12000 — including which were excluded and why), carrageenan/LBG, KCl, CAPS buffer, etc.
Four experimental runs: Experiments 1 & 2, each with/without ATPS-ISPR, with reactor setup (1 L RBR, Spinchem), operation mode, temperature/pH profiles, sampling, and full results (titers, phase concentrations, partition coefficients, yields — e.g. the headline 33.1 g/L pCA at 0.724 g/g yield).
Supporting screening data that doesn't map to core schema fields but is in the paper: the Figure 2 activity-vs-salt dataset, Table 1/Figure 3 ATPS cloud-point and partition-coefficient screens, and the process economics discussion.
Explicit gaps: an not_covered_by_this_paper list flagging what the model asks for that this text simply doesn't report (Km/kcat/Ki values, EC number, sequences, thermodynamics, etc.) — those live in a companion paper (ref. [6]) or the Supporting Information, which wasn't available to me.

No values were invented — anything not stated in the main text is null with a note.